  "worked_solution": "First, notice that we are given that \n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2x-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSubstituting $2x-3y=u$ and $y=v$ into the equation of the first curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2x-3y)^{2}+y=3\\,⟹\\,{u}^{2}+v=3\\,⟹\\,v=3-{u}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhile substituting $y=v$ into the equation of the second curve, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=0\\,⟹\\,v=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the intersections of the curves in the $uv$-plane, we solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}v=3-{u}^{2} \\\\ v=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}u=\\pm \\sqrt{3} \\\\ v=0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection points are $(\\pm \\sqrt{3},0).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14186334/assets/172daaae3de5212c5e182965b66bf2afcade59e2d5eb156c7dbff214e3bfb040.png)\n\nAs a result, our domain in the $uv$-plane has the type I representation \n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}(D)=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\le u\\le \\sqrt{3},\\,0\\le v\\le 3-{u}^{2}\\}.\n$$",
